I then used the predict() function to create table to calculate predicted wage for ages 25-65 for all the regressions and then rbind to make on dataframe.

Finding the peak (max) for each regression, I got the following summary: 
  Group                    Peak_Age Peak_Wage
1 All Full-Time Workers          50     83612
2 College-Educated Workers       52    119477
3 Female                         50     94665
4 Male                           53    142857
5 Non-White Men                  49    129842
6 Non-White Women                48     92683
7 White Men                      54    147616
8 White Women                    51     95624

Summary: 
College-educated workers reach their peak predicted wage at age 52, compared to full-time workers.
College-educated men reach their peak predicted wage at age 53, compared to age 50 for women.
White men have the highest predicted peak wage at age 54, while non-White women have the lowest at age 48.
